    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_7c0dff51a58dcc4d5eadc5e3b0682c0e35c5af2ff549afc5cc5de4a6b08a8dac",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The period integral first compresses the critical L-values into polynomial coefficients; the L-function functional equation then becomes reciprocal pairing of polynomial roots; finally, splitting the resulting reciprocal polynomial into one half and its reflection makes its unit-circle boundary values a real sine or cosine polynomial whose sign changes count the roots.",
