    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_87f472ec3f3ed618296d7d118a2a359c85f588684adfb58200e2c995a20dbf3a",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For the even-sign weight-six case, the endpoint sign condition on Lambda(f,5), Lambda(f,4), and Lambda(f,3) has two complementary explanations: unconditionally, each symmetry orbit of Hadamard zeros satisfies a local inequality that survives multiplication; conditionally on the L-function RH, even-derivative positivity at the center makes the same inequality transparent through Taylor expansion.",
