    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_963a838deaea077c9a910a7376d200a9868558370a986cb65ba5d872cf81ea04",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "After normalizing the period polynomial, the proof isolates an exponential model whose phase winds monotonically and has alternating extrema. A uniform error smaller than the model's minimum boundary amplitude preserves all required sign changes; explicit bounds on the three error sources make this test effective, and a finer local comparison on both sides of each model phase zero upgrades the count to quantitative root localization.",
