    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_987a70b7ea6bdef00e637059f3e2d689f4d32e3047aa7e2c445c3a90723e6206",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The proof makes its coverage boundary explicit: monotone-coefficient zero counting handles moderate weights above level-dependent bounds, while a dominant-phase error estimate handles larger weights and levels. Their uncovered complement is finite, and the source then evaluates critical values and checks either the coefficient criterion or the stronger direct trigonometric sign count rather than extending either analytic estimate beyond its hypotheses.",
