    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_9ba90d5a1abfd181e071b979f9ae6d8097df8c14dc6861dbcc4c45b1e864ae42",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Coarse location and symmetry of completed-L zeros control critical values through symmetry-grouped Hadamard factors, while the Euler product controls ratios of later L-values uniformly in level and weight. After binomial normalization, these two analytic controls supply the ordered coefficients needed to transfer classical trigonometric sign and interlacing results to period-polynomial root geometry; special small-weight inequalities can instead be assembled orbit by orbit.",
